course: dictionary
lesson: 12130
title: Words that help us remember
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word commemorative is built from commemorate, which means to remember something important on purpose. A commemorative object is made so that people will remember a special event or person.
explain: «The town printed a commemorative stamp for its 500th birthday.» The stamp is not just for posting letters. The words 500th birthday show the event, and commemorative tells you the stamp is there to help people remember it.
explain: Look for clue words around the new word. Dates, anniversaries, famous names and words like "plaque" or "coronation" often sit near commemorative. Ask yourself: what is this object for? If the answer is remembering, you have found the meaning.
fact: Commemorative means made or done to help people remember an important event or person.
fact: «A commemorative coin» is a coin made to mark a special event, such as a big anniversary.
fact: Other commemorative things include stamps, plates, plaques and trees planted in memory of someone.
fact: A good check is to swap in "helping people remember" for commemorative. If the sentence still makes sense, you have it right.
fact: Commemorate is the verb: to remember and honour an important event or person.
exercise: «The town made a commemorative coin for its 500th birthday.» Why was the coin made? | To be thrown in a fountain for luck | *To help people remember the birthday | To show the weather | To buy sweets at the shop
exercise: «The school planted a commemorative tree for its founder.» What does commemorative tell you about the tree? | It was planted in winter | It gives the best fruit | It is the tallest tree in the park | *It is there to help people remember someone
exercise: «The museum sold a commemorative plate for the king's coronation.» Find and copy the one word that tells you the plate is for remembering. | *commemorative | plate | sold | museum
test: «The school planted a commemorative tree to honour its first head teacher.» What does commemorative show about the tree? | It will be cut down next year | It was planted by the head teacher's own family | *It is there to help people remember | It is the oldest tree in the area
test: Which of these is a commemorative object? | A pencil for spelling tests | *A plaque put up to mark a famous writer's 100th birthday | A bicycle with two wheels | A bag of crisps
exam: Mia says a commemorative plate is just an ordinary plate for dinner. Is she right? | Yes, it is just for eating dinner off | No, it is made of gold, so it is valuable | Yes, but only at Christmas | *No, it is made to help people remember an important event or person
